WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:17.124
"To battle, boys! Attack!" Peter's voice rang out.

2
00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:22.513
In an instant, the boys raised their weapons and charged the pirates.

3
00:00:22.514 --> 00:00:26.824
Swords clashed and screams pierced the air.

4
00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:33.243
Stunned, the pirates scattered around the deck, and the boys hunted them down in pairs.

5
00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:38.773
Though the pirates were stronger, they were surprised by how fierce the boys were.

6
00:00:38.774 --> 00:00:44.022
Separated and alone, each pirate thought he was the last one alive.

7
00:00:44.023 --> 00:00:49.458
Some jumped into the sea; others hid in the dark corners of the ship.

8
00:00:49.459 --> 00:00:54.917
Tootles, instead of fighting, ran around the deck with a lantern.

9
00:00:54.918 --> 00:00:59.585
He shone his light in the faces of hiding pirates, blinding them.

10
00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:02.138
Then the other boys took over.

11
00:01:02.139 --> 00:01:13.080
Slightly continued to count the victims—five, six, seven, eight, nine. The count grew until they were all dead.

12
00:01:13.081 --> 00:01:17.239
Even John and Michael managed to kill a pirate or two.

13
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:24.663
With his pirates gone, Hook was surrounded by the boys, but he kept them back with his sword and hook.

14
00:01:24.664 --> 00:01:30.754
Then Peter arrived. "Put away your swords, boys," he called.

15
00:01:30.755 --> 00:01:34.010
"This man is mine!"

16
00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:37.980
Face to face, the two enemies stared at each other.

17
00:01:37.981 --> 00:01:41.431
Hook growled, while Peter smiled.

18
00:01:41.432 --> 00:01:48.538
"So, Peter Pan, this is all your doing," said Hook.

19
00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:54.529
"Yes, and this time, it's you or I!" Peter challenged.

20
00:01:54.530 --> 00:02:00.825
"Then prepare to die!" cried Hook.

21
00:02:00.826 --> 00:02:04.561
Their weapons flashed and the battle began!

22
00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:09.205
Peter was an excellent swordsman, fast and precise.

23
00:02:09.206 --> 00:02:14.463
But he was small, and he struggled to get close enough to strike Hook's chest.

24
00:02:14.464 --> 00:02:19.732
Hook, though not quite as quick, was experienced and skilled.

25
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:24.510
But he found it hard to land his blade on his hated foe.

26
00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:30.418
Light as a feather, Peter fluttered around, always avoiding Hook's sword.

27
00:02:30.419 --> 00:02:34.088
Then the captain swung at Peter with the point of his hook.

28
00:02:34.089 --> 00:02:40.167
But Peter ducked under it, lunged forward, and pierced Hook between the ribs.

29
00:02:40.168 --> 00:02:44.056
At the sight of his own blood, Hook dropped his sword.

30
00:02:44.057 --> 00:02:48.399
The boys cried, "Hooray!"

31
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.745
Peter hushed them and invited his foe to pick up his sword.

32
00:02:52.746 --> 00:02:58.354
Humiliated by Peter's display of fairness, Hook was now furious.

33
00:02:58.355 --> 00:03:01.484
He no longer cared whether he won or lost.

34
00:03:01.485 --> 00:03:05.605
All that mattered was that Peter should die.

35
00:03:05.606 --> 00:03:12.731
He rushed to the cannon, known as Long Tom, and hooked a bag of gunpowder with his iron claw.

36
00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:18.319
With his good hand, he held up a lantern, threatening to light the powder with its flame.

37
00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:25.571
"We will all be blown to bits!" Hook screamed.

38
00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:32.295
Like an arrow, Peter flew straight at the bag, grabbed it, and threw it overboard.

39
00:03:32.296 --> 00:03:35.279
Then he marched toward Hook with his dagger.

40
00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.566
Hook sprang onto the rail at the side of the ship and threw himself into the water.

41
00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:48.038
Sadly, the pirate captain was unaware that the crocodile had followed Peter and was swimming around the ship.

42
00:03:48.039 --> 00:03:52.641
That was the last anyone saw of Captain James Hook.

43
00:03:52.642 --> 00:03:56.805
"Hooray!" shouted the boys.

44
00:03:56.806 --> 00:04:00.209
Wendy glowed with pride at Peter's success.

45
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:04.616
The boys crowded around her, and she praised them all equally.

46
00:04:04.617 --> 00:04:10.141
Then she took them into Hook's cabin and pointed to his watch hanging on a nail.

47
00:04:10.142 --> 00:04:16.572
"It's one thirty in the morning!" she said. "You should all be asleep!"

48
00:04:16.573 --> 00:04:21.633
Quickly she got the children to bed in the pirates' bunks and tucked them in.

49
00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:25.997
There was no time for a story, but they didn't need one.

50
00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:31.440
They only had to remember the grand adventure of that very night.

51
00:04:31.441 --> 00:04:34.984
Only Peter stayed up on the deck of the Jolly Roger.

52
00:04:34.985 --> 00:04:42.783
He paced up and down, thinking about Wendy, about her leaving Neverland, and about the trip home.

53
00:04:42.784 --> 00:04:45.233
Finally he fell asleep.

54
00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:49.802
Wendy found him in the night, curled up beside Long Tom.

55
00:04:49.803 --> 00:04:53.558
She bent over and kissed him on the cheek.

56
00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:58.267
The next morning, Peter was the new captain of the Jolly Roger.

57
00:04:58.268 --> 00:05:01.358
The boys took their places as crew.

58
00:05:01.359 --> 00:05:04.558
They even pretended to be pirates for a while.

59
00:05:04.559 --> 00:05:08.010
Peter made a brief speech and everyone cheered.

60
00:05:08.011 --> 00:05:12.736
As the wind filled the sails, they headed for England.

61
00:05:12.737 --> 00:05:17.175
Captain Peter calculated they would reach the coast in a couple of days.

62
00:05:17.176 --> 00:05:29.315
Then they would fly the rest of the way to their final destination—the home of Wendy, John, and Michael.
